  {
   "id": "aXIgQNFHAgAJ",
   "from": "Eric Rexstad",
   "author": "75e0b0abcbafbc7d",
   "date": "2022-06-27T13:10:46Z",
   "subject": "{Disarmed} Re: {Suspected Spam} [distance-sampling] RE: Export/save DSM output/prediction as GIS layer",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nRichard</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nI&#39;m not an expert in DSM nor GIS so this isn&#39;t likely to be a high quality answer.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nNevertheless, I recognise the plotting code as coming from a DSM vignette produced by some of our French colleagues</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<a href=\"http://distancesampling.org/R/vignettes/hare_point_transect_dsm.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://distancesampling.org/R/vignettes/hare_point_transect_dsm.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472509604000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ZF5Qpqu2n-i_lfYui4fvJ\">http://distancesampling.org/R/vignettes/hare_point_transect_dsm.html</a><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"width:100%;margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px;max-width:800px;min-width:424px\">\r\n<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"padding:12px 36px 12px 12px;width:100%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(200,200,200);border-radius:2px\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"border-spacing:0px\" valign=\"top\">\r\n<td style=\"width:100%\">\r\n<div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:300;margin-right:8px;font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_light&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP Light&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:12px\">\r\n<a href=\"http://distancesampling.org/R/vignettes/hare_point_transect_dsm.html\" style=\"text-decoration:none;color:var(--themePrimary)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://distancesampling.org/R/vignettes/hare_point_transect_dsm.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472509604000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ZF5Qpqu2n-i_lfYui4fvJ\"><font color=\"red\"><b>MailScanner has detected a possible fraud attempt from &quot;distancesampling.org&quot; claiming to be</b></font> DSM using point transect data - distancesampling.org</a></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;max-height:100px;color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_normal&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:12px;margin-right:8px;overflow:hidden\">\r\n## Warning: package &#39;knitr&#39; was built under R version 3.3.3. In France, the French National Agency for Hunting and Wildlife has recently created the Hare network (Mauvy et al. 2017), a network of voluntary sites where hares and foxes are sampled every year\r\n in February using point transect sampling (Péroux et al. 1997).. As an illustration, we used the sampling data from Rouillacais for hare ...</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:400;color:rgb(166,166,166);font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_normal&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif\">\r\n<a href=\"http://distancesampling.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://distancesampling.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472509604000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0hI0yiZ5v-RNE8NQFJM-Y2\">distancesampling.org</a></div>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nThe essential objects that you want is either the object created by the function <code>\r\ngrid_plot_obj()</code>​ or the constituent pieces passed as arguments to that function ( `pred.grid` and\r\n<code>mod_tw_pred</code>​).</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nAfraid I don&#39;t know how to export them into GIS layers; the GIS gurus may have thoughts about this.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" style=\"font-size:11pt\" color=\"#000000\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Giliba Richard &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nyan...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 27 June 2022 13:55<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> {Suspected Spam} [distance-sampling] RE: Export/save DSM output/prediction as GIS layer</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"color:#073763\">Hello Distance team,</div>\r\n<div style=\"color:#073763\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"color:#073763\">I wanted to export/save the prediction map generated by DSM (see the ggplot attachment) as a GIS layer (e.g. grid, tiff etc.) so that I can visualize and do map layouts  in arcGIS/ArcMap software.</div>\r\n<div style=\"color:#073763\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"color:#073763\">Is there a way to do it?</div>\r\n<div style=\"color:#073763\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"color:#073763\">Best regards</div>\r\n<div style=\"color:#073763\">Richard</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>\r\n<div>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#385723\">-</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Richard A. Giliba</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">School of Life Sciences and Bio-Engineering </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">\r\n<span style=\"color:black;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:7pt\">The Nelson Mandela African Institution of Science and Technology, Arusha, </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">P.O. Box 447 Arusha, Tanzania.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Cell: <a href=\"tel:+255%20767%20710%20622\" value=\"+255767710622\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+255 767 710 622</a></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#073763\">Email: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"color:blue\">richard...@nm-aist.ac.tz</span></a> </span></p>\r\n<u><span style=\"font-size:7.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:blue\"><span style=\"color:blue\"></span></span></u></div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p><u><span style=\"font-size:7pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:blue;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&amp;user=Smn5kqsAAAAJ&amp;view_op=list_works&amp;sortby=pubdate\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl%3Den%26user%3DSmn5kqsAAAAJ%26view_op%3Dlist_works%26sortby%3Dpubdate&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472509604000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0DJVWK3Lx1E4kzkq9SfA5G\">https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&amp;user=Smn5kqsAAAAJ&amp;view_op=list_works&amp;sortby=pubdate</a></span></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p></p></div></div>"
