     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, 27 Jun 2022 at 22:48, Laura Marshall &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">drlhma...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Richard,<div><br></div><div>I think you are looking to do something like this?</div><div>I&#39;ll use the dsm example code in the R help as a demo<br></div><div><br></div><div>library(Distance)<br>library(dsm)<br><br># load the Gulf of Mexico dolphin data <br>data(mexdolphins)<br><br># fit a detection function and look at the summary<br>hr.model &lt;- ds(distdata, truncation=6000,<br>               key = &quot;hr&quot;, adjustment = NULL)<br><br># fit a simple smooth of x and y to counts<br>mod1 &lt;- dsm(count~s(x,y), hr.model, segdata, obsdata)<br><br># predict over a grid<br>mod1.pred &lt;- predict(mod1, preddata, preddata$area)<br><br><b># Make an XYM sf points object and writes it to shapefile<br>library(sf)<br>p_data &lt;- data.frame(X = preddata$x, Y = preddata$y, M = mod1.pred)<br>points &lt;- st_as_sf(p_data, coords = c(&quot;X&quot;, &quot;Y&quot;, &quot;M&quot;), dim = &quot;XYM&quot;)<br>st_write(points, dsn = &quot;predictions.shp&quot;)</b><br></div><div><br></div><div>Best wishes,</div><div>Laura</div><div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, 27 Jun 2022 at 13:55, Giliba Richard &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nyan...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"color:rgb(7,55,99)\">Hello Distance team,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"color:rgb(7,55,99)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"color:rgb(7,55,99)\">I wanted to export/save the prediction map generated by DSM (see the ggplot attachment) as a GIS layer (e.g. grid, tiff etc.) so that I can visualize and do map layouts  in arcGIS/ArcMap software.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"color:rgb(7,55,99)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"color:rgb(7,55,99)\">Is there a way to do it?</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"color:rgb(7,55,99)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"color:rgb(7,55,99)\">Best regards</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"color:rgb(7,55,99)\">Richard</div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Garamond,serif;color:rgb(56,87,35)\">-</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:7pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:black\">Richard\r\nA. Giliba</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:7pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:black\">School\r\nof Life Sciences and Bio-Engineering </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:black;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:7pt\">The\r\nNelson Mandela African Institution of Science and Technology, Arusha, </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:7pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:black\">P.O. Box\r\n447 Arusha, Tanzania.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:7pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:black\">Cell:\r\n<a href=\"tel:+255%20767%20710%20622\" value=\"+255767710622\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+255 767 710 622</a></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:7pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(7,55,99)\">Email: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"color:blue\">richard...@nm-aist.ac.tz</span></a> </span></p><u><span style=\"font-size:7pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:blue\"><span style=\"color:blue\"></span></span></u></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u><span style=\"font-size:7pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:blue\"><a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&amp;user=Smn5kqsAAAAJ&amp;view_op=list_works&amp;sortby=pubdate\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl%3Den%26user%3DSmn5kqsAAAAJ%26view_op%3Dlist_works%26sortby%3Dpubdate&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472509617000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2XKaBT2zTVLhHxJs6zcxrQ\">https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&amp;user=Smn5kqsAAAAJ&amp;view_op=list_works&amp;sortby=pubdate</a></span></u></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"></span></p></div></div></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;distance-sampling&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance-sampl...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/CALuszxJw_JvO5aF0yj3AJdzE6ncBpyBQ3iNorKkoBVz%3DSEspmQ%40mail.gmail.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/CALuszxJw_JvO5aF0yj3AJdzE6ncBpyBQ3iNorKkoBVz%253DSEspmQ%2540mail.gmail.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472509617000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3